    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33638" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pānĭcĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made of bread</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>huge loaves</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 3, 257</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pānĭcĕus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>an inhabitant of Breadville</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus est Paniceis, milites panicei (a comic
					expression),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 1, 2, 59</span></i>
			.</div>
